[0.005, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H  │ Flushes                          │ 2 per 30 s, plus the hourly snapshot                       │\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B├──────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B│ Lost in a crash               \u001b[38G│\u001b[40GUp\u001b[43Gto\u001b[46G30\u001b[49Gs\u001b[99G│\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B├──────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B│ Recovery                         │ Load the snapshot, replay up to an hour of batches         │\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B└──────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mKept from R03:\u001b[20G\u001b[22mthe \u001b[25Gatch files, catalogue, chain and replay.\u001b[86G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mChanged:\u001b[22m batches are written after the steps have run, each request recorded with the step it ran at, and\u001b[111Greceipts\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gare no longer\u001b[19Gheld \u001b[25Gack.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mR04:\u001b[22m still adds the snapshot and replay from it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BSay go and I'll make that the start of R04, with the flush interval as a setting.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNot measured: Release serialise time, and the real split of the 76 KB per player.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GCrunched for 1m 56s · done 10:10 am\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mSo the current system would only need to write 16gb a day with 256 players?\u001b[39m                                           \r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m*\u001b[3GPerusing… \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[3B\u001b[38