[0.012, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 357 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  a process is killed at each commit boundary, where `cli_serve` kills it between steps.              \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 358 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **R05.** A request queued and never committed gets no answer at shutdown, where the plan asks for   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 359 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  a stopped response; and the limits on what a world may store.                                       \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 360 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **The cadence.** Whether a server with no request queued commits every 21 ms is the user's to       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 361 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  settle: a batch committed for a second's steps ahead would be 1 file a second, and a request        \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 362 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  would then wait for it.                                                                             \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 374 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **R05.** A backup is the directory copied between a flush and the next; the limits on what a world  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 375 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  may store; and a request queued and not yet run at a stop, which gets no answer.                    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 376 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **R09.** The gated test that pins [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mthe state inventory\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](#the-state-inventory) to the names the      \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 377 +\u001b[38;2;